      "content": "It makes complete sense to doubt the value of therapy when you feel empty and disconnected from the very person needing help; your observation that you are rearranging grayness highlights the severity of this dissociation. Please know that this shell-like state is a symptom of a condition, not a character flaw, and many people find relief through specialized programs like EMDR or DBT designed specifically for trauma and numbness. If talking feels impossible right now, simply reaching out to a crisis line just to connect with a human being who doesn't expect you to \"fix\" anything can sometimes be the first small step toward breaking the glass.",
